  "2026-10-09T10:50:57.951Z","harness:codex","{\"text\":\"Duplicate check: strict complete all-status 2908-item corpus (2602 closed, 233 open, 59 draft, 14 canceled; no omissions/unreadable rows), keyword CLI searches, and live full metadata/history reads of pm-ygli86, pm-q7c36n, pm-kvxqp1, pm-lwnifd and pm-agent-token-path. No exact active owner for this regression. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1429\"}"
  "2026-10-09T10:56:36.785Z","harness:codex","TDD baseline: executable workflow preservation test runs the real Bash copy body and the real package-artifact entrypoint from a foreign temporary workspace. It fails with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND for temp-lifecycle.mjs before packaging, matching hosted Release run 37911971128. Existing 30 tests still pass."
  "2026-10-09T11:31:19.995Z","harness:codex","Cross-project intake: strict all-status corpus and live metadata/history preserve historical completed work. All 18 open GitHub issues have PM-link comments; initial open PR, Dependabot, code-scanning and secret-scanning counts were zero. Full graph audit retained 14911 deduplicated edges, 14844 informative, no ordering contradiction or isolated active item; historical hierarchy advisories and 170 missing-resolution warnings remain visible. Fresh required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with no critical/high Sentry findings, and one-day telemetry reports 4830 finishes, 0.87% failures and zero missing error-code rows. These are current observations, separate from hosted release success and permanent queue drainage."
  "2026-10-09T11:40:53.966Z","harness:codex","Full final-source coverage passed 9958 tests with zero uncovered source counts: lines 64101/64101, statements 67275/67275, functions 13870/13870, branches 51487/51487. All owner-linked tests passed through pm test with isolated schema context. Final candidate/control npm and Bun manual sessions each passed 13 steps with real population, complete SDK read, observed refusal/recovery status and original output ceilings. The earlier full run failed a host npm-module resolution prerequisite and remains a failed receipt; enabling the installed global npm module resolved it without changing source or tests. Final static/context/packed consumer chain is running and closure awaits its result."
  "2026-10-09T11:52:50.260Z","harness:codex","Graph admission: reviewed-control recovery shares delivery with portable transcript verification; full coverage and installed public SDK acceptance retain the completed output-budget behavior. The historical installer-diagnostic owner belongs to the same installed-consumer recovery boundary. No completed work is reopened or given an invented dependency."
  "2026-10-09T11:56:29.333Z","harness:codex","After manually validating all eight new holder/target references using the public SDK census, graph-composition passes at 1233 rather than the previous 1236 ceiling. Tightened the existing assertion through pm assurance put, retained its historical owner and exemptions, and updated its positive/negative boundary cases to 1233 pass / 1234 fail. The earlier aggregate static attempt remains failed; all preceding source gates passed, and the graph repair plus remaining component checks are verified separately. Historical gaps remain explicit rather than receiving speculative relations."
  "2026-10-09T12:10:30.186Z","harness:codex","Final pre-PR aggregate validation passed: fresh complete pnpm quality:static, typecheck, source exact coverage, context/token surface, doc/skill links, tracked-file secret scan, dependency audit, all linked checks, npm/npx/Bun/bunx packed consumers and 89-command package-first dogfood. Latest npm pm-changelog 2026.10.5 generated the four actual closures under Unreleased; its check passed. Final distribution 19952672 bytes is below the unchanged 20000000-byte base budget. Historical 170 missing-resolution warnings and known prose gaps remain explicit. All four implemented owners are closed/released; the separately reproduced schema-field transport owner stays open/unclaimed. Hosted review and exact-tag publication recovery remain separate upcoming verifications."
